// input: after idr-simplify
// ack is partial (it recurses on Ints), and `ack 3 n` is not closed, but a
// machine integer is no static shape: ack stays one function, which LLVM may
// specialize on the constant. `count 3` is a closed call of an action that
// writes output: it stays a call, of the clone that runs the action it
// returns, which the world does not make open.
// CHECK-DAG: func.func private @Main.ack(
// CHECK-DAG: call @Main.count$raise${{[0-9]+}}(%{{.*}}, %{{.*}}) : (i64, !idr.world)
// CHECK-NOT: func.func private @Main.ack{{[^(]+}}(
